course: dictionary
lesson: 5634
title: One word, many lines
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word line has many meanings, so the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «Draw a straight line under the answer» means a thin mark on paper. «Wait in line for lunch» means people standing one behind another.
explain: A line can also be a row of writing. «Each line should be a phrase, not just one word» talks about the lines of a poem. A line can be a long string too, like a washing line or a fishing line. Ask yourself which picture fits the sentence best.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the word line. If «a row of people» makes sense, you have got it. If not, try another meaning until the sentence clicks.
fact: As a noun, a line is a row of people or things, one behind another.
fact: As a verb, to line up means to stand in a row.
fact: In maths, a line can be a straight line, a number line or a line of symmetry.
fact: Vikings wrote with runes, which were letters made of straight lines for cutting into wood and stone.
exercise: «Draw a straight line under the answer.» What does line mean here? | * A thin mark on paper | A phone connection | A row of people | A rope for washing
exercise: Mum says, «Please line up at the door.» What should the children do? | Lie down on the floor | * Stand in a row, one behind another | Run home | Sing a song
exercise: «Each line of the poem starts with a letter from the word.» Which meaning of line fits here? | * A row of writing | A washing line | A queue of people | A train route
test: «The washing line was full of wet towels.» What does line mean in this sentence? | A row of people waiting | A row of writing | * A long string or rope | A straight mark on paper
test: «The committee checked the bill line by line.» What does line by line mean here? | * Checking each line one at a time | Without any lines at all | Very quickly, all at once | Drawing lines all over the bill
exam: «The Vikings wrote with runes, letters of straight lines.» In this sentence, what does line mean? | To stand in a row | A row of people | * A straight mark or stroke | A phone connection
